[SECTION]
TITLE: 1. System Overview

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1.1 System Description

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The Flight Management System (FMS) is an integrated avionics system that provides automated flight control, navigation, and performance management for commercial aircraft. The system interfaces with various aircraft sensors, navigation databases, and control surfaces to optimize flight operations.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1.2 System Functions

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-SYS-FUNC-001
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
Automated flight path computation and guidance
<<<

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-SYS-FUNC-002
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
Navigation database management
<<<

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-SYS-FUNC-003
LEVEL: B
STATEMENT: >>>
Performance optimization and fuel management
<<<

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-SYS-FUNC-004
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
Flight plan execution and monitoring
<<<

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-SYS-FUNC-005
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
Interface with autopilot and flight control systems
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1.3 Hardware Components

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
- Flight Management Computer (FMC)
- Control Display Unit (CDU)
- Navigation sensors (GPS, IRS)
- Datalink communication unit
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1.4 Safety Features

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
- Redundant processing channels
- Built-in self-test capabilities
- Fault detection and isolation mechanisms
- Safe mode degradation strategies
<<<

[/SECTION]

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 2. Software Overview

[SECTION]
TITLE: 2.1 Software Description

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The FMS software consists of multiple integrated components responsible for navigation, guidance, performance calculations, and pilot interface. The software implements partitioning to isolate safety-critical functions from less critical operations.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 2.2 Software Components

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-SW-COMP-001
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
**Navigation Manager**

Processes sensor data and computes aircraft position. This component is Design Assurance Level A due to its critical role in providing accurate position information for flight control.
<<<

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-SW-COMP-002
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
**Guidance Controller**

Computes flight path and steering commands. This component is Design Assurance Level A as incorrect guidance could lead to catastrophic failure conditions.
<<<

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-SW-COMP-003
LEVEL: B
STATEMENT: >>>
**Performance Calculator**

Optimizes flight performance and fuel consumption. This component is Design Assurance Level B as performance degradation leads to hazardous conditions.
<<<

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-SW-COMP-004
LEVEL: C
STATEMENT: >>>
**Database Manager**

Manages navigation and airport databases. This component is Design Assurance Level C as database issues cause major operational impacts.
<<<

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-SW-COMP-005
LEVEL: C
STATEMENT: >>>
**Display Interface**

Provides pilot interface and displays. This component is Design Assurance Level C as display failures impact pilot situational awareness.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 2.3 Partitioning Strategy

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The system implements spatial partitioning between Level A navigation and guidance functions and lower criticality functions. Temporal partitioning ensures deterministic execution of safety-critical tasks.

Memory protection mechanisms prevent Level A code from being corrupted by lower-level partitions. Each partition has protected memory regions verified through static analysis.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 2.4 Redundancy Mechanisms

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The FMS implements dual-channel redundancy with cross-channel monitoring. Independent processing channels execute identical software with comparison logic to detect and isolate faults.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3. Certification Considerations

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.1 Software Design Assurance Level

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The software is classified as **Design Assurance Level A** per DO-178C.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.2 Failure Conditions and Software Contribution

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-FAIL-001
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
**Failure Condition:** Total loss of navigation capability
**Classification:** Catastrophic
**Software Contribution:** Software failure leading to incorrect position computation could result in loss of navigation, potentially causing loss of aircraft control.
<<<

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-FAIL-002
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
**Failure Condition:** Misleading navigation information
**Classification:** Hazardous
**Software Contribution:** Software error causing incorrect guidance commands could mislead flight crew, resulting in hazardous flight conditions.
<<<

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-FAIL-003
LEVEL: B
STATEMENT: >>>
**Failure Condition:** Loss of performance optimization
**Classification:** Major
**Software Contribution:** Performance calculator malfunction could result in inefficient fuel usage and operational limitations.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.3 Deactivated Code

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
No deactivated code is present in the delivered software configuration. All code is active and verified according to Level A requirements.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 4. Software Lifecycle

[SECTION]
TITLE: 4.1 Lifecycle Model

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The software follows a modified V-model lifecycle with iterative development phases. Requirements flow from system to software to design, with corresponding verification activities at each level.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 4.2 Software Lifecycle Processes

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-PROC-001
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
**Software Planning Process**

Establishes plans for development, verification, configuration management, and quality assurance.
<<<

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-PROC-002
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
**Software Development Process**

Transforms requirements into verified software through requirements analysis, design, and coding.
<<<

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-PROC-003
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
**Software Verification Process**

Demonstrates correctness and completeness through reviews, analyses, and testing.
<<<

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-PROC-004
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
**Software Configuration Management Process**

Controls and tracks software items throughout the lifecycle.
<<<

[PLAN]
UID: PSAC-PROC-005
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
**Software Quality Assurance Process**

Provides confidence that processes are performed correctly.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[/SECTION]

