[SECTION]
TITLE: 6. Schedule

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The following milestones are planned for the certification program:

**Software Requirements Review** - 2024-03-15
- Software Requirements Data (SRD)
- Requirements traceability to system requirements

**Software Design Review** - 2024-06-30
- Software Design Description (SDD)
- Low-level requirements traceability

**Code Complete** - 2024-09-30
- Source code baseline
- Unit test results

**Software Integration Complete** - 2024-11-15
- Integration test results
- Software/hardware integration results

**Software Verification Complete** - 2025-01-30
- Software Verification Results (SVR)
- All verification evidence

**Certification Audit** - 2025-03-15
- Software Accomplishment Summary (SAS)
- All lifecycle data
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 7. Additional Considerations

[SECTION]
TITLE: 7.1 Previously Developed Software

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The FMS reuses navigation algorithms from a previously certified system (Level B). This software will be reverified to Level A standards with additional structural coverage analysis and robustness testing.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 7.2 Tool Qualification

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The following development tools require qualification per DO-330:
- Compiler: Qualified as TQL-5 (verification tool)
- Static analyzer: Qualified as TQL-5 (verification tool)
- Requirements management tool: Does not require qualification (no credit taken)
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 7.3 Alternative Methods

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Formal methods will be applied to the navigation state machine to demonstrate correctness per DO-333 supplement. This will satisfy certain verification objectives with analysis rather than testing.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[/SECTION]

